        "original_id": "db0a45fb-9f15-53c9-a7ea-43f89354c2a4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jaroslav Kvapil, Antonín Dvořák, Jan Hus\n- Places: Chudenice, Prague, Kingdom of Bohemia, Central Europe\n- Works: Rusalka\n- Movements: Hussites, Bohemian Reformation\n- Topics: Czech Republic\n\nFacts:\n- The Kingdom of Bohemia was a medieval and early modern monarchy in Central Europe and the predecessor of the modern Czech Republic.\n- The Hussites were a pre-Protestant Christian movement that began in the Kingdom of Bohemia.\n- The Hussites followed the teachings of Czech reformer Jan Hus, who became the best known representative of the Bohemian Reformation.\n- Jaroslav Kvapil was born on 25 September 1868 in Chudenice in the Kingdom of Bohemia.\n- Jaroslav Kvapil was a Czech poet, playwright, and librettist.\n- Rusalka is an opera described as a lyric fairy tale by Antonín Dvořák.\n- Jaroslav Kvapil died on 10 January 1950 in Prague.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
